            <ArticleTitle>Short-term intervention reduces bioelectrical impedance analysis-measured visceral fat in type 2 diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e27-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2013.12.046</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0168-8227(13)00480-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 25 patients with Type 2 diabetes mellitus, the short-term in-hospital calorie restriction combined with moderate exercise reduced visceral fat. The reduction of visceral fat can improve metabolic cardiovascular risk factors, while the reductions in body weight and waist circumference were small and reduction in subcutaneous fat was not significant.</AbstractText>
